  <section class="content-block">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 class="text-center section-title">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <div class="faq-section">
        <div class="faq-item">
          <h3>How much space do I need for a basketball court?</h3>
          <p>A regulation full court requires 94 feet × 50 feet, but most residential courts are half-courts ranging from 30 feet × 30 feet minimum to 50 feet × 40 feet for optimal play. We can design courts to fit your available space while maintaining proper proportions.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <h3>Can I install a basketball hoop on an existing driveway?</h3>
          <p>Yes, if the driveway has adequate space and is in good condition. We can add court lines, install permanent hoops, and enhance the surface for better ball handling. Asphalt driveways may need resurfacing for optimal play.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <h3>What's the difference between adjustable and fixed-height hoops?</h3>
          <p>Adjustable hoops allow height changes for players of different ages and skill levels, typically ranging from 7.5 to 10 feet. Fixed-height hoops are set at regulation 10 feet and offer greater stability and durability for serious play.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <h3>How do I maintain a basketball court?</h3>
          <p>Regular maintenance includes cleaning debris, power washing, checking for cracks, and refreshing line markings every few years. Proper drainage and prompt crack repair prevent major issues and extend court life significantly.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <h3>Can I add other sports to my basketball court?</h3>
          <p>Absolutely! Basketball courts work well with pickleball, volleyball, street hockey, and other sports. We can design multi-sport line configurations using different colors to clearly distinguish each sport's boundaries and rules.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

